<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024_exam 36</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024_EXAM 36 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 4/26<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 43 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T07:39:30.404Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which black-box technique should be used to verify different responses of the system, depending on its current conditions or previous history?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Use case testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Decision table testing</div><div class="opt correct">c. State transition testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Equivalence partitioning</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.2 State transition testing, câu hỏi là kỹ thuật nào kiểm tra phản hồi khác nhau của hệ thống dựa vào điều kiện hoặc lịch sử phía trước ( trạng thái trước đó) chỉ có mỗi kỹ thuật là state transition thôi</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">In addition to thorough testing of the requirements specification, a development team aims to involve users as early as possible in the development process, using practices such as prototyping, to ensure that the software systems being developed will meet the users’ expectations. This approach is especially useful at mitigating the risks associated with one of the seven testing principles, which one?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Tests wear out. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Absence-of-errors fallacy. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Working software over comprehensive documentation.</div><div class="opt ">d. Defects cluster together.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.3. 7 nguyên lý test. Câu hỏi là đội phát triển đã mời user vào giai đoạn sớm của quy trình phát triển, để đảm bảo là phần mềm đc xây đúng với mong muốn của user. Cách này giúp giảm thiểu rủi ro theo nguyên lý test nào?</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">Determining the schedule for each testing activity and test milestones for a test project, using activity estimates, available resources, and other constraints is a typical task performed during:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test execution. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test design.</div><div class="opt ">c. Test analysis.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Test planning. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a typical potential risk of using test automation tools?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Reduced feedback times regarding software quality compared to manual testing. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Reduced test execution times compared to manual testing.</div><div class="opt ">c. Reduced repeatability and consistency of tests compared to manual testing.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Underestimation of effort required to maintain test scripts. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 6.2. Câu hỏi là cái nào là rủi ro tiềm ẩn của automation test tool? cái này tra sách. Cái A,B,C hiểu là benefit vì nó giúp giảm thời gian, giảm lặp lại. Còn D từ Underestimation là thiếu effort để maintain test scripts nên D là risk</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">The following decision table is used to assist a doctor in determining the drug therapy to prescribe for a patient (aged 6 to 65 years) diagnosed with acute sinusitis. The table consists of three Boolean conditions and six actions (image) Based only on the given information, which of the following statements is TRUE?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Column 7 represents an impossible situation and thus can be deleted. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Columns 1 and 3 can be merged into a single column.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Columns 2, 4, 6 and 8 can be merged into a single column. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Columns 5 and 7 can be merged into a single column.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2 Bảng decision table. Chúng ta gộp các cột mà kết quả nó giống nhau, sau đó nhìn lên input xem có 1 cái nào nó quyết định kết quả này còn các input khác T hay F ko quan trọng là ta gộp đc</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a factor that contributes to a successful review?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. All participants in the review are aware they will be evaluated based on the defects they will find. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The author of the work product to be reviewed leads the review meeting.</div><div class="opt correct">c. All participants in the review are trained to deal with the review type and its objectives. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Review metrics must be collected to improve the review process.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.4 Success factors. Đọc lại sách nhớ lại mấy keyword chính như objective, time, notification, training, management support. Nhờ thế ta chọn đc C là Những người tham gia review đc đào tạo để làm việc với các review type khác nhau</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following correctly represents a test first approach?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Tests are derived from acceptance criteria and run to check that the code passes these tests [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Application behaviour is written in Given/When/Then format and tests are then written and run</div><div class="opt ">c. Code is refactored first then tests are written and run</div><div class="opt correct">d. First the tests fail then the code is written to pass the tests and this is iterated [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1 Test first. Cái nào sau đây đúng? Các bạn đọc định nghĩa test first là viết TC trước khi viết code nên ta chọn đc D. Test viết trước, chạy test fail, rồi code đc viết để pass test. Còn các đáp án khác chỉ là 1 loại của test first thôi như A là ATDD, B là nói format viết test case của BDD và ATDD, C là của TDD</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an example of a shift left?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Performing non-functional testing using functional test cases [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Monitoring system performance after the release</div><div class="opt correct">c. Using Acceptance Test-Driven Development [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Participating in retrospectives</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1 Shift left. Cái nào là ví dụ của shift left. ta nhẩm lại lý thuyết nhé: early test, test first, CI/CD, automation test, static analysis tool... trong các đáp án trên chỉ có C là đang nói về test first và automation. còn D là retrospective ko phải, B after release là quá muộn, A ko thể test non-functional mà lại dùng test case của functional đc</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT an example of a test-first approach to development?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Acceptance Test-Driven Development [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test Coverage-Driven Development [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Behavior-Driven Development</div><div class="opt ">d. Test-Driven Development</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1 dễ quá</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements BEST describes the difference between testing and debugging?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing causes failures while debugging fixes failures [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing is a negative activity while debugging is a positive activity</div><div class="opt correct">c. Testing determines that defects exist while debugging removes defects [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Testing finds the cause of defects while debugging fixes the cause of defects</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.2 khác biệt giữa debug và test là gì? Test tìm lỗi, debug loại trừ lỗi</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">(image) This user story and its associated acceptance criteria contain which of the following typical defects identified by static testing in this type of work product?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Deviation from standards [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Contradiction [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Security vulnerability</div><div class="opt ">d. Coverage gaps</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a technique used in machine learning?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. State transition testing ( Decision tree) [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Equivalence partitioning</div><div class="opt ">c. Boundary value analysis</div><div class="opt ">d. Decision tables</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a true statement about test automation scripts that are captured using a capture/replay tool?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The scripts are easy to maintain [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The scripts are data-driven</div><div class="opt correct">c. The scripts may be unstable [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The scripts are created by experienced automators</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following program fragment: if day = Monday then statement a else statement b end if if day = Tuesday then statement c end if What is the minimum number of test cases needed to achieve 100% statement coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 2 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 3</div><div class="opt ">d. 4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">You are defining the process for carrying out product risk analysis as part of each iteration on an Agile project. Which of the following is the proper place to document this process in a test plan?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Scope of testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Approach of testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Metrics of testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Configuration management of the test object</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">You are reading a user story in the product backlog to prepare for a meeting with the product owner and a developer, noting potential defects as you go. Which of the following statements is true about this activity? (Select Two)</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. It is not a static test, because static testing involves execution of the test object [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. It is not a static test, because static testing is always performed using a tool [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">c. It is a static test, because any defects you find could be found cheaper during dynamic testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt correct">d. It is a static test, because static testing does not involve execution of the test object [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is MOST likely to be an example of a PRODUCT risk?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. The expected security features may not be supported by the system architecture. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. The developers may not have time to fix all the defects found by the test team</div><div class="opt ">c. The test cases may not provide full coverage of the specified requirements.</div><div class="opt ">d. The performance test environment may not be ready before the system is due for delivery</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following tasks is MOST LIKELY to be performed by the test manager?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Write test summary reports based on the information gathered during testing [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Review tests developed by other</div><div class="opt ">c. Create the detailed test execution schedule</div><div class="opt ">d. Analyze, review, and assess requirements, specifications and models for testability</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements CORRECTLY describes a role for impact analysis in maintenance? ( Select two)</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Impact analysis is used when deciding if a fix to a maintained system is worthwhile [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. Impact analysis is used to identify how data should be migrated into the maintained system [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">c. Impact analysis is used to decide which hot fixes are of most value to the user</div><div class="opt correct">d. Impact analysis is used to optimize the scope of regression test [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">As a result of risk analysis, more testing is being directed to those areas of the system under test where initial testing found more defects than average. Which of the following testing principles is being applied?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Beware of the pesticide paradox [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing is context dependent</div><div class="opt ">c. Absence-of-errors is a fallacy</div><div class="opt correct">d. Defects cluster together [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following is the BEST definition of a waterfall model?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Defining requirements, designing software and testing are done in phases where in each phase a piece of the system is added [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing is viewed as a separate phase which takes place after development has been completed</div><div class="opt correct">c. A phase in the development process should begin when the previous phase is complete [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. A phase in the testing process should begin when the previous phase is complete</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following describes the difference between test reporting and test control in the context of the ISTQB Foundation syllabus?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test reporting invokes corrective actions; test control only gathers metrics. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test reporting collects information and gives feedback; test control is about guiding or corrective actions based on that information. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test reporting happens only after execution; test control only before execution.</div><div class="opt ">d. Test reporting ensures the tests are designed correctly; test control ensures the tests are executed correctly.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statement is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test report: changing the test schedule due to availability of the test environment [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test report: providing a summary information of what has been tested [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test control: summarising the number of test cases executed during the test period.</div><div class="opt ">d. Test control: collects information and gives feedback</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Which TWO of the following activities should be completed before the test execution?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Preparing the test environment [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedright">b. Writing and reviewing test cases [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Logging test incidents</div><div class="opt ">d. Analyzing test results</div><div class="opt ">e. Re-testing fixed defects</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following is a key benefit of using a test charter in an exploratory testing session?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. It replaces all scripted test cases. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. It provides guidance, objectives and scope while preserving tester freedom. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. It documents expected results for every possible input.</div><div class="opt ">d. It ensures that no defects will be found.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">Which Software Development Lifecycle in CTFL v4.0 is more flexible over than the V-model?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Model-based development lifecycle [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Waterfall lifecycle</div><div class="opt correct">c. Incremental lifecycle [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Sequential lifecycle</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div></body></html>